  "body": "Eastern Beach has always had a way of making people want to stay. The sea air, relaxed pace and coastal lifestyle which creates a sense that you've found somewhere worth putting down roots.\r\n\r\nNow, for the first time in years, five new architecturally designed homes have arrived on one of East Auckland's most sought-after coastal streets - offering a rare opportunity to secure a home by the beach.\r\n\r\nDesigned with modern coastal living in mind, each home brings together open-plan living, contemporary kitchens, quality finishes and low maintenance spaces that make everyday life easy.\r\n\r\nWith five homes and a choice of layouts, there is genuine flexibility for different lifestyles. Whether you're a growing family looking for space, a professional wanting a quality coastal base, downsizing and ready to simplify or an investor seeking something different, this development offers an opportunity worth exploring. Each residence features three bedrooms, two bathrooms and allocated off-street parking, with a high level of specification throughout.\r\n\r\nBeyond the homes, the location adds another layer to everyday life. Backing onto Rogers Park and the Clovelly walkway network, you'll have green space and outdoor connection right at your doorstep. Eastern Beach playground and Macleans Park are just a few minutes' walk away, making it easy to bring more of the weekend into everyday life, from morning walks and playground adventures to running, cycling and time in or by the water.\r\n\r\nFor families, the schooling is another key advantage. The homes are zoned for Bucklands Beach Primary, Bucklands Beach Intermediate and Macleans College, providing a sought-after local schooling pathway from primary through to secondary years.\r\n\r\nFive homes - one exceptional coastal address.\r\n\r\nMetres to the beach, beautifully designed and ready for a new chapter - this is Eastern Beach living, made new.\r\n\r\n* Terms & conditions apply.\r\n\r\n*Find more properties you may like at https://www.teamvishrealestate.co.nz",
